  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nSimplify: 15 (3)/(4) - 6 (4)/(5) + 4 (25)/(3)\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nConvert mixed numbers to improper fractions and perform arithmetic operations.\n\n**Calculations:**\n\n15 (3)/(4) = (15 × 4 + 3)/(4) = (60 + 3)/(4) = 63/4\n\n6 (4)/(5) = (6 × 5 + 4)/(5) = (30 + 4)/(5) = 34/5\n\n4 (25)/(3) = (4 × 3 + 25)/(3) = (12 + 25)/(3) = 37/3\n\n⇒ Simplify: (63/4) - (34/5) + (37/3)\n\nFind common denominator (LCM of 4, 5, 3 is 60):\n\n⇒ (63/4) = (63 × 15)/(4 × 15) = 945/60\n\n⇒ (34/5) = (34 × 12)/(5 × 12) = 408/60\n\n⇒ (37/3) = (37 × 20)/(3 × 20) = 740/60\n\n⇒ Combine fractions: (945/60) - (408/60) + (740/60)\n\n⇒ (945 - 408 + 740)/60\n\n⇒ 1277/60\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (4).**",
